55	//  SG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL — the per-cell GEMM-engine selector (DESIGN-TC-PIPELINE.md
56	//  §9 / the owner "BOTH paths compiled, the tuner picks" directive). The scalar
57	//  fp32 owner-computes path (model_stages_decoder.cuh) and the bf16 wgmma
58	//  tensor-core path (model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh) are compiled ALONGSIDE each
59	//  other; the kernel-autotuner injects -DSG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL=<token> per-TU to
60	//  pick one. Absent the macro, the SCALAR path compiles verbatim (CONTRACT
61	//  rule 3: an untuned build is a correct build) — this is the shipped default
62	//  and the path all of test_megakernel_vs_eager.py's L3-REAL decoder gates
63	//  exercise; adding this seam must leave those numbers BIT-IDENTICAL.
64	//
65	//  Tokens are integers (the C preprocessor cannot compare strings, and the
66	//  autotuner's -D injection passes an integer literal):
67	//      SG_GEMM_IMPL_SCALAR = 0   (default; the verbatim fp32 path below)
68	//      SG_GEMM_IMPL_WGMMA  = 1   (the Fork-B bf16 tensor-core cell)
69	//
70	//  WGMMA-PATH STATUS (honest, no-suppression — MEMORY.md "fix components, never
71	//  disable them"): the validated unit today is the GEMM ENGINE
72	//  (model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh::tc_gemm_block_unpipelined + the wgmma.cuh /
73	//  tile_pipeline.cuh substrate), silicon-gated 13/13 by test_decoder_tc.py
74	//  (fwd/dX/dW vs the bf16-rounded fp64 oracle, A=I localizations exactly 0.0,
75	//  dW A/A/A bit-identical) on a validated 18/18 substrate. The full Fork-B
76	//  fwd+bwd CELL DRIVER (the phase-restructured P0→P1(fwd+bwd, acts→HBM)→
77	//  optimizer megakernel that REPLACES the body below) is DESIGN §11 work item
78	//  R2.3 and is NOT yet authored. Selecting the wgmma token therefore FAILS THE
79	//  COMPILE LOUDLY (the #error below) rather than silently shipping the scalar
80	//  body under a wgmma name — a wgmma-requested cell that secretly ran scalar
81	//  would be exactly the functionality suppression the owner forbids. The seam
82	//  is in place and dormant; wiring the driver into it is the bounded next step.
83	// ============================================================================
